==Spanish==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|es|bacallao}}
* {{alt|es|bacalado||nonstandard|hypercorrection}}

===Etymology===
From {{der|es|nl|bakaliaw}}, {{der|es|odt|bakeljauw}}, {{m|odt|kabeljauw}}, of {{unc|es|nocap=1}} origin.  Possibly from {{der|es|la|baculum||stick, staff}}, referring to the way cod were split and dried on wooden sticks.  Or, possibly borrowed or influenced by {{bor|es|eu|bakailao}}, which could be related to the Dutch word.

Cognate with {{cog|it|baccalà}}, {{cog|pt|bacalhau}}, {{cog|gl|bacallau}}, {{cog|ca|bacallà}}.

